{
  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200 is strongest (accuracy ~0.65, F1 ~0.63), while image-only ResNet50 singleprofile is weak (accuracy 0.208, F1 0.172), leaving it unclear whether image features are useful at all or whether multiprofile aggregation can improve them. This experiment tests image-only multiprofile ResNet50 with avgpool, the aggregation that already works well for RNA, to isolate whether profile/aggregation improves the image modality before adding fusion. It is the best next budget use because it is a minimal extension of the only image baseline, avoids confounding fusion and RNA-encoder choices, and will clarify whether multimodal experiments with ResNet50 are worth pursuing or whether a different image encoder should be tested."
}

